Company Comments:
(1/16/2026) Harbor Freight Tools: Harbor Freight appreciates the submitter for bringing their concerns to our attention. Harbor Freight takes all safety concerns seriously. 

The Bauer 14 Tooth 4 Wood Carving Disc (Carving Disc) is a double saw-tooth carving tool intended for sculpting, channeling, hollowing, and cutting curves in wood. The Carving Disc is intended for use with 4 in. and 4-1/2 angle grinders. Wood carving is a common and popular hobby, but it is also one that carries risk if safety measures are not followed. As with all Harbor Freight products, the Carving Disc should be operated in a manner consistent with the warnings and instructions contained on the packaging and in the user manual. Users should only use the Carving Disc if they have read and are familiar with these important warnings and instructions. The Carving Disc can be used safely when operated and maintained in accordance with the user instructions and warnings.

The instructions provided with the Bauer Carving Disc teach the proper way to setup, operate, and maintain the carving disc. These include:
1)	Installing the disc on a 4? or 4-1/2? angle grinder equipped with a paddle switch, with a 5/8? spindle, and a maximum speed of 14,000 RPM or less;
2)	Threading the auxiliary handle onto the LEFT side of the grinder and using only in  right-hand operation;
3)	Rotating the angle grinder safety guard such that it is at a 45 degree angle with respect to the right side of the body of the grinder;
4)	Allowing the tool to reach full speed before making contact with the workpiece;
5)	Cutting by pulling the grinder back towards you, not pushing away from you; and
6)	Operating the product away from the face or the head.

Harbor Freight strongly encourages all users to always wear proper PPE when carving wood and working with products such as the Carving Disc. This includes wearing ANSI-approved eye and hearing protection, as well as heavy duty work gloves at all times. 

The submitter of this report references a warning contained in the manual for angle grinders not to attach wood carving discs. All Harbor Freight angle grinders carry warnings and instructions consistent with industry standards that specifically explain how to avoid injuries associated with kickback. When used incorrectly, a chainsaw wood carving disc may result in kickback.

Harbor Freight notes that the risk of injury described by the submitter includes reference to events involving a variety of similar wood carving products associated with brands other than Harbor Freights Bauer branded Carving Disc. The types of injuries described by the submitter can occur when a disc is accidentally used incorrectly, as referenced by the submitter. Such risks of injury may be avoided by wearing proper PPE and following all product warnings and instructions. The submitter also states the Carving Disc works great when used one way. Harbor Freight emphasizes such use is in a manner consistent with the Carving Discs warnings and instructions. 

Harbor Freight appreciates the submitter reporting their concerns and encourages all users to read and carefully follow all warnings and safety instructions. Users with questions about the Bauer Carving Disc, or any other Harbor Freight product, are encouraged to  contact Harbor Freight directly at 800-444-3353 or productcompliance@harborfreight.com.
